<style>
  body {
    /* NO font-size. This frame inherits the document's root from the overlay
       stylesheet `api-cloudrun` injects at the top of this partial
       (`injectPartDefaults`), so the footer is whatever size the quote is —
       9px today via `styles/quote.css`, and automatically right if that moves.
       It used to hardcode 10px, which was correct only by coincidence and went
       silently wrong the day the quote became a 9px document (templates#114).
       `color` stays: it is this partial's own choice, not the page's.

       ⚠️ Do NOT write the literal opening head tag anywhere in this file, in a
       comment or otherwise. `injectPartDefaults` finds its insertion point with
       a regex over the whole string, so a mention of it in prose is matched as
       if it were the document's own — and the entire overlay is spliced INTO
       this comment. Cost me a render that showed the stylesheet as body text. */
    color: #121212;
  }
  a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: #121212
  }
  footer {
    font-size: 1rem;
    width: 100%;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    /* 1rem of clear air between the last line of the body and the first line
       of this footer. It has to be bought HERE, not with `margin_bottom`:
       Chromium hangs the body content edge and the footer frame off the same
       band top, so raising the bottom margin moves BOTH and the gap does not
       change. Measured before this rule, the footer reached 2pt ABOVE the
       body content edge (754pt vs 756pt on letter) — the ~16px that usually
       separates them was slack in the last line box, not a rule, and a page
       whose content filled the column had them touching.
       12px, and deliberately ABSOLUTE rather than `rem`. The gap above the
       footer is a fact about the PAGE — how much clear air sits between the last
       body line and this band — so it must not move when the document's font
       size does. (It was absolute for a second reason that is now gone: this
       partial used to render with no stylesheet at all, so `rem` meant
       Chromium's default rather than the quote's root. Since
       `injectPartDefaults` the frame does inherit the overlay, and `1rem` here
       would now track the quote — which is exactly what this rule does not want.)
       `margin_bottom` moved 0.5 -> 0.62in in the same change, which is what
       keeps this padding from pushing the footer into the paper edge. The two
       cancel: measured on letter, the footer ink still runs 754..775pt, exactly
       where it sat before, 0.22in clear of the paper. Raising the band alone
       would have moved the content edge with it and bought nothing; padding
       alone would have driven the ink to 0.11in, inside the no-print zone of
       most desktop printers. */
    padding-top: 12px;
  }
  div {
    padding: .25em 0;
    width: 100%;
  }
  #fein, #pages {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
  }
  #pages, #contacts {
    justify-self: end;
    text-align: right;
  }
  #email {
    padding-right: 1em;
    border-right: 1px solid #eee;
  }
  #phone {
    padding-left: 1em;
  }
</style>
<footer>
  <div id="fein">FEIN: 92-0918396</div>
  <div id="pages">Page <span class="pageNumber"></span> of <span class="totalPages"></span></div>
  <div id="website"><a href="https://www.chicagofilmsupplies.com">https://www.chicagofilmsupplies.com</a></div>
  <div id="contacts">
    <a id="email" href="mailto:team@chicagofilmsupplies.com">team@chicagofilmsupplies.com</a>
    <a id="phone" href="sms:+13128183008">312.818.3008</a>
  </div>
</footer>
